@c -*-texinfo-*-
@node math-dsp Manual
@chapter Crate @code{math-dsp}
@cindex math-dsp
@cindex DSP utilities

@code{math-dsp} (library name @code{math_audio_dsp}) is the shared DSP
toolbox: signal generation, FFT analysis, EBU R128 loudness, ReplayGain,
ESPRIT, STFT, RTPGHI phase reconstruction, audio features. It feeds the
engine, the plugin host and the recorder.

@menu
* math-dsp User Guide::
* math-dsp Developer Guide::
@end menu

@node math-dsp User Guide
@section User Guide

End users experience this crate indirectly:

@itemize @bullet
@item Loudness meter and EBU R128 measurement in the desktop player.
@item ReplayGain scanning of the library.
@item Waveform thumbnails in the queue / library.
@item Test signals generated by @code{generate-audio-tests}.
@end itemize

@node math-dsp Developer Guide
@section Developer Guide

@subheading Modules

@multitable @columnfractions .25 .75
@headitem Module @tab What it does
@item @code{signals} @tab Test signals (tones, sweeps, noise) with
  fade / padding / channel utilities.
@item @code{analysis} @tab FFT analysis (Welch / single-FFT), RT60,
  C50/C80, THD, mic compensation, CSV I/O.
@item @code{simd} @tab SIMD-optimised DSP primitives.
@item @code{stft} @tab Short-Time Fourier Transform.
@item @code{rtpghi} @tab Real-time phase gradient heap integration
  (phase reconstruction from magnitude STFT).
@item @code{ebur128} @tab EBU R128 / ITU-R BS.1770-4 loudness.
@item @code{binaural_loudness} @tab BS.1770-4 for 2-ch headphone
  signals; BS.775 surround->binaural downmix presets (5.0 / 5.1 / 7.1)
  and custom matrix path.
@item @code{esprit} @tab ESPRIT sinusoidal frequency estimation.
@item @code{instantaneous_frequency} @tab Instantaneous frequency from
  analytic signal.
@item @code{tonal_transient} @tab Tonal-vs-transient separation.
@item @code{fdn} @tab Feedback Delay Network reverberation.
@item @code{fast_math} @tab Fast approximations (exp, log, pow).
@item @code{audio_features} @tab Chroma, spectral features, tempo,
  loudness, zero-crossing rate.
@item @code{replaygain} @tab ReplayGain analyser
  (@code{ReplayGainAnalyzer}, @code{compute_album_gain}).
@item @code{waveform} @tab Waveform-visualisation data
  (@code{compute_waveform}).
@end multitable

@subheading Determinism

Math utilities are deterministic given the same input; tests rely on
golden buffers for the signal generators and golden CSV files for
analysis routines.

@subheading Testing

@example
cargo test -p math-dsp
@end example
